1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,140
I'm ready to crush this.

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,080
Let's go!

3
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:49,420
I'm sure it feels that way, but he has a reason for everything.

4
00:00:51,660 --> 00:00:53,700
I can't give up on being a forward.

5
00:00:54,280 --> 00:00:56,060
It's who I am, and I'm not budging.

6
00:00:56,060 --> 00:01:01,400
I'll give Fullback a try, but if I want out, I'll need to know.

7
00:01:03,600 --> 00:01:05,020
What he was thinking!

8
00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:07,060
What the hell?!

9
00:02:38,032 --> 00:02:42,532
Oh, Tachibana's like 40 miles away.

10
00:02:42,952 --> 00:02:44,892
The field seems so much bigger than before.

11
00:02:45,632 --> 00:02:45,972
Huh?

12
00:02:46,792 --> 00:02:47,832
The shuffle.

13
00:02:49,392 --> 00:02:51,572
If you can manage to get that down,

14
00:02:51,992 --> 00:02:55,112
then I don't care if you go and join the attack or stay out here.

15
00:02:56,612 --> 00:02:58,412
The ball's all the way upfield.

16
00:02:58,892 --> 00:03:00,472
This is not the time to be defending.

17
00:03:01,352 --> 00:03:02,532
I'm pushing up.

18
00:03:02,992 --> 00:03:04,532
Owie! Get back here!

19
00:03:05,672 --> 00:03:06,612
Wait, what?

20
00:03:06,612 --> 00:03:09,812
You said it didn't matter if I stayed here or joined the attack.

21
00:03:09,952 --> 00:03:11,492
Idiot, look at the other wing.

22
00:03:11,852 --> 00:03:14,692
See how Masako, the right back, is already pushing up?

23
00:03:14,872 --> 00:03:18,452
If the far right back goes forward, the left back drops into the middle, remember?

24
00:03:18,972 --> 00:03:21,612
Togashi and I have already shuffled across, so you stay put.

25
00:03:22,012 --> 00:03:25,292
Don't just push up without checking to see what your teammates are doing first.

26
00:03:31,032 --> 00:03:31,872
Hey, Otomo!

27
00:03:33,972 --> 00:03:35,332
Oh, damn it all!

28
00:03:35,332 --> 00:03:36,852
They're coming!

29
00:03:37,612 --> 00:03:40,132
Not that this is something I didn't already know,

30
00:03:40,532 --> 00:03:42,472
but I absolutely hate defending!

31
00:03:42,592 --> 00:03:43,792
I hate it more than anything!

32
00:03:44,512 --> 00:03:44,732
Huh?

33
00:03:45,852 --> 00:03:47,212
They're coming down the left.

34
00:03:47,532 --> 00:03:49,032
Does that mean they're targeting me?

35
00:03:49,752 --> 00:03:51,972
Okay, shift across and cover the middle.

36
00:03:52,212 --> 00:03:52,652
Got it!

37
00:03:53,312 --> 00:03:54,832
All right, you guys, I'm ready!

38
00:03:55,172 --> 00:03:56,252
Come at me, you punks!

39
00:03:56,272 --> 00:03:57,252
I'm waiting for you!

40
00:03:57,252 --> 00:03:59,092
What the hell are you doing, Ewie?

41
00:03:59,512 --> 00:04:01,192
You're supposed to be shuffling, idiot!

42
00:04:06,072 --> 00:04:07,292
That's how I got here?

43
00:04:07,712 --> 00:04:08,112
Look!

44
00:04:08,312 --> 00:04:09,852
I shuffled across like you said!

45
00:04:10,052 --> 00:04:11,472
That is not what you're doing!

46
00:04:11,472 --> 00:04:13,692
He can't be serious!

47
00:04:13,992 --> 00:04:17,952
If I keep moving further across, I'll be leaving the wing wide open!

48
00:04:17,952 --> 00:04:24,452
It's like you have zero awareness at all of what you need to play defense.

49
00:04:24,912 --> 00:04:27,752
I didn't know I had to teach you the basic rules of each position.

50
00:04:28,512 --> 00:04:28,952
Unbelievable.

51
00:04:28,952 --> 00:04:36,032
You can't play the same way here you play up front, Ewie.

52
00:04:36,412 --> 00:04:38,992
When you run out, no one is behind you to guard the goal.

53
00:04:40,052 --> 00:04:41,112
Repeat after me.

54
00:04:41,372 --> 00:04:42,352
There is no one.

55
00:04:43,232 --> 00:04:44,072
Think you got it?

56
00:04:44,392 --> 00:04:46,692
Repeat that to yourself until the next ball comes.

57
00:04:47,712 --> 00:04:48,192
Ashito!

58
00:04:49,132 --> 00:04:51,692
You aren't shuffling into the middle at all, man.

59
00:04:52,232 --> 00:04:53,652
We have to tighten up more.

60
00:04:54,312 --> 00:04:55,492
Make that the priority.

61
00:04:55,492 --> 00:04:59,492
Uh-huh, uh...

62
00:05:00,072 --> 00:05:05,332
Ashito!

63
00:05:06,252 --> 00:05:06,692
What?

64
00:05:07,572 --> 00:05:10,292
This is the first time I've even touched the ball today!

65
00:05:10,932 --> 00:05:12,312
Let's try to build some momentum!

66
00:05:12,672 --> 00:05:13,632
Let's go!

67
00:05:15,012 --> 00:05:18,532
Don't just push up without checking to see what your teammates are doing first!

68
00:05:19,032 --> 00:05:20,472
Hang on, Masako!

69
00:05:21,072 --> 00:05:22,452
He's not moving up.

70
00:05:23,112 --> 00:05:24,152
He's staying put.

71
00:05:24,692 --> 00:05:25,312
I'm out!

72
00:05:25,492 --> 00:05:26,012
Yeah?

73
00:05:28,572 --> 00:05:29,332
Look out!

74
00:05:29,392 --> 00:05:30,752
The A-team defender is pressing!

75
00:05:31,372 --> 00:05:32,852
The midfielder, too!

76
00:05:33,872 --> 00:05:34,932
I'm surrounded!

77
00:05:35,532 --> 00:05:37,232
Ashito, put the ball out!

78
00:05:37,532 --> 00:05:38,932
Nah, it's too late!

79
00:05:43,972 --> 00:05:44,572
Akutsu!

80
00:05:44,832 --> 00:05:46,392
He's cutting into the space on the left!

81
00:05:46,392 --> 00:05:51,052
There are still two forwards hanging out in the middle.

82
00:05:51,052 --> 00:05:52,272
I can't cover him!

83
00:05:52,272 --> 00:06:09,372
Whether I push up or stay back, I gotta base that decision on everyone else.

84
00:06:09,372 --> 00:06:11,252
And I'm supposed to shuffle across.

85
00:06:11,252 --> 00:06:13,672
But I don't know how far to go in!

86
00:06:13,672 --> 00:06:15,532
I'm not meant for this position!

87
00:06:15,532 --> 00:06:18,612
And I'm absolutely bored out of my mind!

88
00:06:19,232 --> 00:06:20,772
What the hell's that old man thinking?

89
00:06:20,772 --> 00:06:22,732
He was dead wrong!

90
00:06:22,732 --> 00:06:24,732
There's no way I can do this!

91
00:06:24,732 --> 00:06:32,892
What's up, guys?

92
00:06:32,892 --> 00:06:35,972
You think the poor B-team is gonna be okay?

93
00:06:35,972 --> 00:06:39,392
We don't have much room to talk since we lost Yoshitsune.

94
00:06:39,932 --> 00:06:42,112
But your team's fallen apart.

95
00:06:42,112 --> 00:06:47,132
It's like you guys totally forgot how to play when Taita and Nagano aren't around.

96
00:06:47,712 --> 00:06:50,432
And what's with making a complete scrub, the new defender?

97
00:06:52,472 --> 00:06:57,212
Whatever you do, you don't want to get dumped from the Tokyo Metropolis League.

98
00:06:58,352 --> 00:07:00,132
Here's some advice for free, Aoi.

99
00:07:00,492 --> 00:07:01,212
Me to you.

100
00:07:02,352 --> 00:07:06,572
Why don't you go back to your dorm room as soon as possible and start packing up your bags?

101
00:07:07,352 --> 00:07:08,692
The sooner the better.

102
00:07:09,112 --> 00:07:11,452
That lack of talent isn't a good look on anyone.

103
00:07:12,112 --> 00:07:15,352
There's nothing fulfilling about playing as a fullback.

104
00:07:15,752 --> 00:07:17,512
It's so boring.

105
00:07:17,952 --> 00:07:19,412
I can't do this anymore.

106
00:07:19,892 --> 00:07:21,272
It's not right.

107
00:07:21,892 --> 00:07:23,852
This isn't where I ought to be.

108
00:07:27,772 --> 00:07:29,472
Rowan, to the right!

109
00:07:31,872 --> 00:07:33,232
Out there.

110
00:07:33,552 --> 00:07:34,872
That's where I belong.

111
00:07:35,372 --> 00:07:36,152
My spot.

112
00:07:36,612 --> 00:07:37,752
I want to score.

113
00:07:38,652 --> 00:07:39,992
Hey, Aoi, stay put.

114
00:07:40,732 --> 00:07:42,092
Masaka's already pushing up.

115
00:07:42,112 --> 00:07:44,392
Are we going to have to go over this again?

116
00:07:47,452 --> 00:07:48,272
You know?

117
00:07:48,932 --> 00:07:52,572
When you were playing forward, you always seemed like a player with wider vision.

118
00:07:53,012 --> 00:07:56,212
Is that something that just goes away if you're not feeling it, or what?

119
00:07:56,212 --> 00:07:59,492
This isn't where I ought to be.

120
00:07:59,492 --> 00:08:01,552
This isn't where I ought to be.

121
00:08:01,552 --> 00:08:03,872
This isn't where I ought to be.

122
00:08:03,872 --> 00:08:04,872
Shut up, dammit!

123
00:08:04,872 --> 00:08:06,012
Shut up, dammit!

124
00:08:06,492 --> 00:08:07,632
You're in the middle of a game.

125
00:08:08,132 --> 00:08:09,752
Stop freaking out and focus.

126
00:08:13,092 --> 00:08:13,572
Incoming!

127
00:08:14,032 --> 00:08:15,492
Ashito, they got the ball!

128
00:08:19,032 --> 00:08:20,912
You're supposed to shuffle across!

129
00:08:20,912 --> 00:08:23,872
Here comes the shot!

130
00:08:24,192 --> 00:08:24,772
Block it!

131
00:08:29,332 --> 00:08:29,972
Optimo!

132
00:08:30,612 --> 00:08:31,872
It's not over yet.

133
00:08:32,032 --> 00:08:33,132
The ball's not clear!

134
00:08:33,132 --> 00:08:42,012
What is up with this guy's body?

135
00:08:46,752 --> 00:08:47,212
Dammit!

136
00:08:47,472 --> 00:08:48,672
Went to their side again!

137
00:08:48,672 --> 00:08:57,272
Nice clearance!

138
00:08:57,632 --> 00:08:58,412
Corner kick!

139
00:08:59,132 --> 00:09:00,412
Ultimo, are you okay?

140
00:09:01,412 --> 00:09:02,972
Oh, come on, you guys.

141
00:09:03,192 --> 00:09:04,412
No rough stuff today.

142
00:09:04,412 --> 00:09:07,232
Oh, jeez.

143
00:09:07,412 --> 00:09:09,072
This is just only a minigame.

144
00:09:09,712 --> 00:09:12,432
But hey, I guess you all hate to lose.

145
00:09:12,952 --> 00:09:13,912
Am I right?

146
00:09:14,912 --> 00:09:15,852
I'm sorry.

147
00:09:16,192 --> 00:09:17,732
I should have been defending there.

148
00:09:18,092 --> 00:09:18,212
Huh?

149
00:09:18,772 --> 00:09:19,052
Huh?

150
00:09:20,632 --> 00:09:23,252
How about we all play defense today?

151
00:09:24,952 --> 00:09:28,232
I've got a bunch of unused defensive skills that I'd love to show off.

152
00:09:28,752 --> 00:09:30,312
So yeah, this is all for me.

153
00:09:32,892 --> 00:09:34,172
Anyway, we're good.

154
00:09:34,412 --> 00:09:35,832
You should apologize to Togashi.

155
00:09:36,792 --> 00:09:40,072
He wants to play upfield, but he's been too busy defending today.

156
00:09:40,552 --> 00:09:40,892
You know?

157
00:09:45,752 --> 00:09:47,512
Alright, let's restart.

158
00:09:49,312 --> 00:09:50,892
Hey, guys, quit pushing.

159
00:09:51,232 --> 00:09:52,352
I said stop that.

160
00:09:52,732 --> 00:09:55,532
We can't afford any more injuries, so you two cut it out.

161
00:09:56,432 --> 00:09:57,492
Uh, Togashi?

162
00:09:57,892 --> 00:09:58,372
What?

163
00:09:59,092 --> 00:10:00,832
I, uh, I'm sorry.

164
00:10:01,412 --> 00:10:02,392
Because of me?

165
00:10:02,392 --> 00:10:04,892
You can't go upfield like you usually do.

166
00:10:04,932 --> 00:10:06,012
What in the hell?

167
00:10:06,372 --> 00:10:09,392
You think you have any effect on what I do, knucklehead?

168
00:10:10,192 --> 00:10:12,672
I'm the only one who influences how I play.

169
00:10:13,392 --> 00:10:16,972
Fukuda told me I needed to work on my defensive skills, so I am.

170
00:10:16,972 --> 00:10:21,352
I apologize to Otomo, not me.

171
00:10:21,352 --> 00:10:34,772
This isn't where I ought to be.

172
00:10:34,772 --> 00:10:36,572
I know that.

173
00:10:37,112 --> 00:10:39,032
This isn't where I ought to be.

174
00:10:39,572 --> 00:10:40,752
I said I know!

175
00:10:41,032 --> 00:10:41,652
Stop it!

176
00:10:41,652 --> 00:10:45,212
This isn't where I ought to be.

177
00:10:45,212 --> 00:10:46,692
I said I get it!

178
00:10:48,772 --> 00:10:50,012
I get it.

179
00:10:50,392 --> 00:10:52,332
So don't let yourself become a burden.

180
00:10:52,652 --> 00:10:54,052
On your friends!

181
00:11:02,112 --> 00:11:02,872
Farsight!

182
00:11:03,032 --> 00:11:04,612
They're targeting Akutsu!

183
00:11:04,612 --> 00:11:06,612
Even further than that?

184
00:11:06,612 --> 00:11:07,792
But who's it going to?

185
00:11:11,072 --> 00:11:12,412
It's the other flank!

186
00:11:12,852 --> 00:11:13,192
Crap.

187
00:11:13,572 --> 00:11:16,492
They piled players up on the left, hoping this would happen.

188
00:11:23,532 --> 00:11:25,252
Your team's 1 yen coins.

189
00:11:25,732 --> 00:11:27,052
10 yens are the opposition.

190
00:11:27,752 --> 00:11:30,252
You scored because of all the loose balls you picked up.

191
00:11:30,892 --> 00:11:32,072
Were you aware of that?

192
00:11:32,072 --> 00:11:42,172
Did he ride the flight of the ball?

193
00:11:42,832 --> 00:11:43,532
No way!

194
00:11:43,792 --> 00:11:44,852
This was more than that.

195
00:11:45,392 --> 00:11:48,832
The moment he made the corner kick, he started running straight at me.

196
00:11:49,552 --> 00:11:53,492
Your dumbass keeps making dumbass moves, and it's just disgusting!

197
00:12:00,312 --> 00:12:00,872
Go!

198
00:12:00,872 --> 00:12:01,872
Tachibana!

199
00:12:02,492 --> 00:12:03,652
There's only one defender!

200
00:12:03,952 --> 00:12:05,272
It's our best chance to counter!

201
00:12:09,992 --> 00:12:11,492
Okay, time's up!

202
00:12:19,872 --> 00:12:20,992
Yo, B-team.

203
00:12:21,712 --> 00:12:23,752
You have got to ditch that crap defender.

204
00:12:24,232 --> 00:12:27,352
He's only being forced to play defense now to make up the numbers.

205
00:12:27,872 --> 00:12:29,272
But he'll quit soon enough.

206
00:12:29,272 --> 00:12:33,052
You shouldn't hang around talentless, spoiled crybabies.

207
00:12:33,192 --> 00:12:35,532
You could end up just like him if you're not careful.

208
00:12:36,912 --> 00:12:40,772
Like I said, make sure you don't get dropped from the league.

209
00:12:40,992 --> 00:12:44,012
That's literally the only job the second team has.

210
00:12:44,012 --> 00:12:47,412
You should really start worrying about yourselves.

211
00:12:47,412 --> 00:12:52,752
You guys only managed to score one goal against our makeshift talentless team.

212
00:12:53,132 --> 00:12:54,812
What's that say about you?

213
00:12:55,232 --> 00:12:56,912
You're lost without Yoshitsune!

214
00:12:57,272 --> 00:12:59,432
At least that's what it looks like from out here.

215
00:12:59,972 --> 00:13:01,612
Am I right or am I right?

216
00:13:01,612 --> 00:13:08,492
I guess weaklings have to surround themselves with other weaklings.

217
00:13:08,832 --> 00:13:09,092
Huh?

218
00:13:09,532 --> 00:13:14,912
I know that people say it all the time, but I hope you sad sacks haven't been taking it to heart too much.

219
00:13:16,792 --> 00:13:20,752
About how youth teams aren't as strong mentally as high school teams are.

220
00:13:20,752 --> 00:13:30,572
Damn it.

221
00:13:30,932 --> 00:13:32,492
That last clearance.

222
00:13:33,232 --> 00:13:34,752
Why didn't it get to Tachibana?

223
00:13:35,032 --> 00:13:36,672
We could have scored easily.

224
00:13:37,472 --> 00:13:40,472
Feels like your tempo and rhythm are all over the place, huh?

225
00:13:40,472 --> 00:13:43,572
Well, don't overthink it.

226
00:13:44,172 --> 00:13:47,532
And something to remember about the shuffle.

227
00:13:48,312 --> 00:13:53,592
Even if leaving the wing wide open is a big risk, always think about tightening up centrally first.

228
00:13:54,252 --> 00:13:56,652
As long as we have the numbers we need in the middle,

229
00:13:57,032 --> 00:14:00,452
the other team attacking down the flanks isn't going to be that big of a deal.

230
00:14:00,872 --> 00:14:02,992
Well, you'll pick it up soon enough.

231
00:14:03,712 --> 00:14:06,372
So, you brought a girl to training?

232
00:14:06,372 --> 00:14:08,272
Hey, now.

233
00:14:08,512 --> 00:14:11,972
I'm the kind of guy who likes to keep his private life off the soccer field.

234
00:14:12,612 --> 00:14:13,932
Yeah, sure.

235
00:14:22,392 --> 00:14:26,932
Anyway, your shuffle has a way to go, but that last move wasn't bad.

236
00:14:27,292 --> 00:14:28,412
What last move?

237
00:14:28,792 --> 00:14:30,612
Are you talking about the messed up kick?

238
00:14:30,892 --> 00:14:31,212
No.

239
00:14:31,672 --> 00:14:32,312
Before that.

240
00:14:33,332 --> 00:14:33,852
For real.

241
00:14:34,472 --> 00:14:35,772
Your vision's really wide.

242
00:14:36,652 --> 00:14:36,972
Huh?

243
00:14:38,232 --> 00:14:39,752
What do you mean, my vision?

244
00:14:41,332 --> 00:14:43,452
Your lack of self-awareness is intriguing.

245
00:14:44,072 --> 00:14:46,512
You should work on that and be more intentional with it.

246
00:14:46,612 --> 00:14:47,512
You'll have more fun.

247
00:14:48,052 --> 00:14:52,372
I also think it'll help you be less erratic, which could benefit you in all kinds of situations.

248
00:14:52,772 --> 00:14:54,932
I have no idea what you're talking about.

249
00:14:55,512 --> 00:14:57,532
Maybe study Kuribayashi's place.

250
00:14:57,972 --> 00:14:59,112
Have you watched him much?

251
00:15:00,912 --> 00:15:01,272
Huh?

252
00:15:01,272 --> 00:15:06,372
There's some things in his game that you could incorporate into your own.

253
00:15:07,132 --> 00:15:11,532
He's always using techniques to help increase the options he has available to him.

254
00:15:12,372 --> 00:15:14,692
I bet you could increase your options as well.

255
00:15:14,692 --> 00:15:19,572
I think if you do that, playing defense will be a lot more fun.

256
00:15:20,572 --> 00:15:21,532
Later.

257
00:15:21,532 --> 00:15:21,852
Wait.

258
00:15:22,352 --> 00:15:22,672
Wait.

259
00:15:22,672 --> 00:15:23,272
Oh.

260
00:15:23,272 --> 00:15:24,272
Oh...

261
00:15:44,072 --> 00:15:44,772
Yuma.

262
00:15:45,572 --> 00:15:46,772
Hey, what's up?

263
00:15:46,772 --> 00:15:48,272
Togashi, you too.

264
00:15:49,072 --> 00:15:50,272
Can you tell me something?

265
00:15:50,272 --> 00:15:52,272
Why is Aoi playing as a fullback?

266
00:15:53,272 --> 00:15:58,272
The two of you were the first ones to recognize the unique ability that Aoi has.

267
00:15:58,272 --> 00:16:02,272
So then, you must have some idea what's going on.

268
00:16:02,272 --> 00:16:05,272
Why was he suddenly switched to fullback?

269
00:16:05,272 --> 00:16:07,272
What was the purpose?

270
00:16:07,272 --> 00:16:09,272
Is this manager Fukuda?

271
00:16:09,272 --> 00:16:12,272
Is he trying to tell us something?

272
00:16:12,272 --> 00:16:15,272
I'd like to know your honest thoughts on it.

273
00:16:15,272 --> 00:16:20,272
If he's trying to convey a message, I hope you'll tell me.

274
00:16:20,272 --> 00:16:21,272
Ugh.

275
00:16:21,272 --> 00:16:23,272
What the hell are you yakking about?

276
00:16:23,272 --> 00:16:25,272
I'm too beat up for all this.

277
00:16:25,272 --> 00:16:28,272
I get that you're the owner's daughter and all, but damn.

278
00:16:28,272 --> 00:16:31,272
I don't have time to sit here and indulge you nosy rich people.

279
00:16:31,272 --> 00:16:33,272
Now go on home.

280
00:16:33,272 --> 00:16:37,272
Togashi, I can't let you tear her down like this, so I'll fill you in.

281
00:16:38,272 --> 00:16:41,272
Someday, she's gonna be your manager.

282
00:16:44,272 --> 00:16:47,272
And just because she's never played the game doesn't mean she can't be a manager.

283
00:16:48,272 --> 00:16:49,272
Whole new world.

284
00:16:49,272 --> 00:16:52,272
Must be a nice way to live.

285
00:16:52,272 --> 00:16:55,272
Being born to the owner of a soccer team.

286
00:16:55,272 --> 00:17:00,272
Just so we are clear, I never said I wanted to be Esperion's manager.

287
00:17:00,272 --> 00:17:04,272
Which means, this has nothing to do with whose daughter I am.

288
00:17:04,272 --> 00:17:07,272
I want to work with a men's soccer team.

289
00:17:07,272 --> 00:17:08,272
That much is true.

290
00:17:08,272 --> 00:17:10,272
But not a leftover.

291
00:17:10,272 --> 00:17:13,272
It's important to me to build my own career.

292
00:17:13,272 --> 00:17:15,272
Using my own ideas.

293
00:17:15,272 --> 00:17:18,272
Even if it means starting with a smaller team at first.

294
00:17:18,272 --> 00:17:20,272
That's what I've dreamed from myself.

295
00:17:20,272 --> 00:17:21,272
Oh.

296
00:17:25,272 --> 00:17:26,272
It never gets old!

297
00:17:26,272 --> 00:17:28,272
Doesn't matter how many times I hear it.

298
00:17:28,272 --> 00:17:30,272
I love listening to her talk about it.

299
00:17:30,272 --> 00:17:33,272
She's been reciting that fairy tale to us for years!

300
00:17:33,272 --> 00:17:37,272
Okay, fine. I'll tell you.

301
00:17:37,272 --> 00:17:39,272
But let me hear your thoughts first.

302
00:17:40,272 --> 00:17:44,272
Why do you think you made Ashito become a defender?

303
00:17:44,272 --> 00:17:47,272
If you meant what you said, then tell me.

304
00:17:47,272 --> 00:17:49,272
I did, yes.

305
00:17:50,272 --> 00:17:52,272
I'll be honest with you.

306
00:17:52,272 --> 00:17:55,272
At first, I didn't think Aoi was youth team material.

307
00:17:55,272 --> 00:17:58,272
It did not matter to me what position he played.

308
00:17:58,272 --> 00:18:01,272
He'll be a liability to the team.

309
00:18:01,272 --> 00:18:06,272
But after watching the game against Seikyo Hai, I changed my mind.

310
00:18:07,272 --> 00:18:10,272
His vision is truly incredible.

311
00:18:11,272 --> 00:18:15,272
Up till then, I'd never seen a player like him.

312
00:18:15,272 --> 00:18:16,272
Ain't that the truth.

313
00:18:16,272 --> 00:18:21,272
Ashito was brought in to be a fullback cause his vision can be put to best use there.

314
00:18:21,272 --> 00:18:23,272
I'm positive that's why he got in.

315
00:18:23,272 --> 00:18:27,272
Cause let's face it, dude was not the best player that tried out that day.

316
00:18:27,272 --> 00:18:29,272
But that's Fukuda for you.

317
00:18:29,272 --> 00:18:32,272
Please know I haven't changed my mind about our discussion.

318
00:18:32,272 --> 00:18:35,272
I still don't agree with the theories you introduced.

319
00:18:35,272 --> 00:18:38,272
They're not based on scientific fact.

320
00:18:38,272 --> 00:18:40,272
That's a bit of a leap.

321
00:18:40,272 --> 00:18:42,272
He can't know all of your placements.

322
00:18:42,272 --> 00:18:44,272
I hope you understand.

323
00:18:44,272 --> 00:18:46,272
It's impossible.

324
00:18:46,272 --> 00:18:52,272
We should avoid introducing unscientific theories and hypotheses into any sport.

325
00:18:52,272 --> 00:18:55,272
Aoi can memorize some players' positions.

326
00:18:55,272 --> 00:18:57,272
And even predict the movements of others.

327
00:18:57,272 --> 00:18:59,272
But that's it.

328
00:18:59,272 --> 00:19:01,272
That's the scope of his vision.

329
00:19:01,272 --> 00:19:07,272
And for what it's worth, I don't believe his talent is best utilized as a forward.

330
00:19:07,272 --> 00:19:12,272
I honestly think the best position for Aoi is midfielder.

331
00:19:12,272 --> 00:19:14,272
Attacking midfielder.

332
00:19:14,272 --> 00:19:16,272
Or at least a deep line one.

333
00:19:16,272 --> 00:19:18,272
Something central.

334
00:19:18,272 --> 00:19:20,272
But defender makes no sense.

335
00:19:20,272 --> 00:19:24,272
I mean defense isn't remotely in his wheelhouse.

336
00:19:24,272 --> 00:19:27,272
I respect manager Fukuda so very much.

337
00:19:27,272 --> 00:19:30,272
But I have no idea what he was thinking.

338
00:19:30,272 --> 00:19:32,272
I would like to know, though.

339
00:19:33,272 --> 00:19:34,272
Uh, miss?

340
00:19:34,272 --> 00:19:35,272
Do you mean her?

341
00:19:35,272 --> 00:19:37,272
Here's what I've learned.

342
00:19:37,272 --> 00:19:39,272
You really love soccer, don't you?

343
00:19:40,272 --> 00:19:43,272
I've never heard a woman go on about soccer like that.

344
00:19:43,272 --> 00:19:45,272
Oh, yes.

345
00:19:45,272 --> 00:19:47,272
Your passion's legit.

346
00:19:47,272 --> 00:19:49,272
Practically dripping out your nose.

347
00:19:50,272 --> 00:19:52,272
It's too bad.

348
00:19:52,272 --> 00:19:54,272
You're wasting a golden opportunity.

349
00:19:54,272 --> 00:19:55,272
What?

350
00:19:56,272 --> 00:19:57,272
Yeah, I agree.

351
00:19:57,272 --> 00:20:01,272
Honestly, I couldn't care less why Ashito has to be a fullback or whatever.

352
00:20:01,272 --> 00:20:05,272
But I do know I'll never get these past five minutes back where I could've been-

353
00:20:05,272 --> 00:20:06,272
Wait!

354
00:20:06,272 --> 00:20:08,272
Please elaborate on what you just said.

355
00:20:08,272 --> 00:20:14,272
So first of all, you're trying to convince me that what we said in the classroom was unscientific.

356
00:20:14,272 --> 00:20:17,272
Well, I was watching this show a while back.

357
00:20:18,272 --> 00:20:22,272
And they had this ex-Spanish international guy on it as a guest.

358
00:20:22,272 --> 00:20:27,272
They were trying to scientifically prove how wide his field of vision was.

359
00:20:27,272 --> 00:20:29,272
They strapped a small camera to him.

360
00:20:30,272 --> 00:20:31,272
Made him play a match.

361
00:20:32,272 --> 00:20:35,272
And then asked him to review the footage afterwards.

362
00:20:37,272 --> 00:20:39,272
Then they would stop the footage part of the way through.

363
00:20:39,272 --> 00:20:49,272
While it was off, he was told he had to draw the positions of the players at the moment that was last on screen as accurately as possible.

364
00:20:50,272 --> 00:20:53,272
They did the same experiment with other players.

365
00:20:54,272 --> 00:20:58,272
The best they could do was come up with maybe three of them tops.

366
00:20:58,272 --> 00:21:01,272
Some of them barely remembered where they were themselves.

367
00:21:01,272 --> 00:21:05,272
But this guy, he got every player's position perfect.

368
00:21:06,272 --> 00:21:07,272
Both his team and the others.

369
00:21:08,272 --> 00:21:10,272
I know of that experiment.

370
00:21:11,272 --> 00:21:14,272
But that was the product of his training, built on top of his natural talent.

371
00:21:15,272 --> 00:21:17,272
Only special people like him could-

372
00:21:17,272 --> 00:21:22,272
The thing is, none of it matters to the players.

373
00:21:23,272 --> 00:21:24,272
We don't got time for science.

374
00:21:25,272 --> 00:21:29,272
All we care about is what's happening on the field, and we trust our own senses.

375
00:21:30,272 --> 00:21:36,272
You know, Henri, when you were talking about how you didn't think Ashito should be playing fullback,

376
00:21:37,272 --> 00:21:40,272
that you think he ought to be playing centrally, attacking midfielder,

377
00:21:41,272 --> 00:21:44,272
all it made me see is that you don't know that much about soccer.

378
00:21:44,272 --> 00:21:50,272
You seem to think that fullbacks are only there to support, like the Lance and Shogi or something.

379
00:21:51,272 --> 00:21:52,272
Middle's the most important.

380
00:21:53,272 --> 00:21:55,272
That's just your unconscious bias.

381
00:21:57,272 --> 00:22:00,272
No one knows what's up with old man Fukuda's mind.

382
00:22:01,272 --> 00:22:02,272
But we're not talking about him.

383
00:22:03,272 --> 00:22:06,272
You gotta loosen up your thoughts, friend, or you'll miss the big picture.

384
00:22:08,272 --> 00:22:10,272
Soccer's freer! It does what it wants!

385
00:22:11,272 --> 00:22:18,272
That said, I don't want to leave you hanging with what I think about Ashito's on-field position future,

386
00:22:19,272 --> 00:22:23,272
or why I think manager Fukuda reassigned him to play fullback instead of being a forward.

387
00:22:24,272 --> 00:22:28,272
I don't know your opinion, but I bet it's the same as mine.

388
00:22:28,272 --> 00:22:31,272
One, two, three!

389
00:22:32,272 --> 00:22:33,272
Playmaker!

390
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:27,666
Next time on Awashi, just like you.

